### ============================================
### SETUP — create ~5 bookmarks first
### ============================================

### Create bookmark 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://spring.io",
  "title": "Spring Framework"
}

### Create bookmark 2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-boot",
  "title": "Spring Boot Docs"
}

### Create bookmark 3
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://www.postgresql.org",
  "title": "PostgreSQL"
}

### Create bookmark 4
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://flywaydb.org",
  "title": "Flyway"
}

### Create bookmark 5
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://www.docker.com",
  "title": "Docker"
}


### ============================================
### CRUD — DEMO REQUESTS
### ============================================

### List all bookmarks, page 0, size 10 (defaults)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks

### List with explicit pagination — page 0, size 2
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks?page=0&size=2

### List page 1, size 2 — should show different bookmarks than page 0
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks?page=1&size=2

### Get a single bookmark by id — update the id to match what you got back from create
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks/1

### Get a bookmark that doesn't exist — expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks/9999

### Update a bookmark — full replace
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://spring.io/projects/spring-framework",
  "title": "Spring Framework (Updated)"
}

### Update a bookmark that doesn't exist — expect 404
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks/9999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://x.com",
  "title": "X"
}

### Delete a bookmark — expect 204, no body
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks/8

### Delete the same bookmark again — expect 404 (idempotency check)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks/5


### ============================================
### VALIDATION — DEMO REQUESTS
### ============================================

### Create with blank title — expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com",
  "title": ""
}

### Create with blank url — expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "",
  "title": "Missing URL"
}

### Create with both blank — expect 400 with both fields flagged
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "",
  "title": ""
}

### Create with whitespace-only title — @NotBlank should still catch this
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com",
  "title": "   "
}

### Create with malformed JSON body — expect 400 (Jackson parse failure)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

not valid json

### Update with blank fields — expect 400, same validation as create
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "",
  "title": ""
}

### Negative page number — expect 400, not 500 with a stack trace
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks?page=-1&size=2

### Zero size — expect 400
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks?size=0

### Negative size — expect 400
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks?size=-5

### Non-numeric page — expect 400 (Spring's own type conversion failure)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks?page=abc

### Non-numeric id on path variable — expect 400
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookmarks/abc